==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
From {{der|en|grc|γαστήρ||belly}} + {{der|en|grc|ἔντερον||intestine}} + {{der|en|grc|-λογία}}; synchronically, {{affix|en|gastro-|entero-|-logy}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The study of the [[digestive]] system, from mouth to anus. May also include the study of accessory organs: pancreas, liver, gallbladder and bile ducts.

